  "notes": "Names are exactly as INE publishes them: upper case with NO accents or diacritics (e.g. SOFIA, LUCIA, MARTIN, ALVARO, MARIA, JESUS). Rank = row order in the INE file (the file has no rank column; it is sorted by count descending); tied counts are numbered sequentially in file order, not as shared ranks (ties: JESUS/VICTOR 545 male; EVA/LAURA 498 and ELIA/HELENA 282 female). Counts are births in 2024, not people alive; the sheet's TOTAL row (163,732 boys; 154,273 girls) is all 2024 births of that sex, not only the top 100. Compound names: none of the 200 entries contains a space or hyphen; the newborn file lists names as INE publishes them and the methodology for how compound registered names are tabulated was not stated in the file (no explanatory note found for the newborn series). Regional-language names appear in the national top 100 where numerous Spain-wide (e.g. male MARC, PAU, BIEL, NIL, MARTI, ALEX, JAN). INE's separate residents file (nombres_mas_frecuentes.xlsx, census 01/01/2025, people alive, with compound names such as MARIA CARMEN as separate entries) was downloaded for comparison only and not used because it skews older. Source file: nomnac24.xlsx, 43,319 bytes, fetched directly with curl (no API needed); the INEbase page also offers earlier years 2002-2023 with the same layout.",
  "source_id": "src_name_frequency_es_es_ine"
}
